@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - System Statistics and Thread Configuration

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor Administrator
participant "Web UI / CLI" as Client
participant "REST API" as API
participant "SearchController" as Controller
participant "IndexBuilder" as Builder
participant "ThreadPool" as Pool
participant "InvertedIndex" as Index
participant "StatisticsService" as Stats

== Configure Thread Count ==

Administrator -> Client: Select thread count (N)
Client -> API: POST /api/index {"threads": N}
activate API

API -> Controller: buildIndex(N)
activate Controller

Controller -> Builder: buildIndex(N)
activate Builder

Builder -> Pool: createPool(N)
activate Pool
Pool --> Builder: Pool ready
deactivate Pool

Builder -> Builder: Start parallel indexing

note right of Builder
Documents are processed
by N worker threads.
end note

Builder --> Controller: Indexing completed
deactivate Builder

Controller --> API: Indexing result
deactivate Controller

API --> Client: JSON {status, time_ms}
deactivate API

Client --> Administrator: Display build time

== View System Statistics ==

Administrator -> Client: Request statistics
Client -> API: GET /api/stats
activate API

API -> Controller: stats()
activate Controller

Controller -> Stats: collectStatistics()
activate Stats

Stats -> Index: getDocumentCount()
Index --> Stats: Document count

Stats -> Builder: getLastBuildTime()
Builder --> Stats: Build time

Stats -> Builder: getThreadCount()
Builder --> Stats: Threads used

Stats --> Controller: Statistics data
deactivate Stats

Controller --> API: JSON statistics
deactivate Controller

API --> Client: {documents, index_build_time_ms, threads_used}
deactivate API

Client --> Administrator: Display statistics
@enduml